Am I lost again (just when I thought I had this figured out!)?  What's
40%?  I assumed (and we all know what happens when you assume too
much) that 8% of all items generated would be tools, and that of those
(4% large box, 3.5% chest, 3.5% sack, 0.5% oilskin sack, 2% bag of 
holding) 13.5% would be containers.

Ack! Unfortunately the nubmer of items per container varies with the
type of the container.  
   large box   4% prob, 0-3 items (1.5 av)
   chest     3.5% prob, 0-5 items (2.5 av)
   sack      0.5% prob, 0-1 item  (0.5 av)
   o.s.sack  0.5% prob, 0-1 item  (0.5 av)
   BOH         2% prob, 0-1 item  (0.5 av)

So on average a tool contains .04*1.5+.035*2.5+.03*.5 = 0.1625 other items.

